%!PS
% The text of testdata/pdffontreal/gs-reencoded.pdf: Ghostscript 10.08 made the
% PDF with
%   gs -q -dNOPAUSE -dBATCH -sDEVICE=pdfwrite -dCompatibilityLevel=1.4 \
%      -dEmbedAllFonts=true -dSubsetFonts=true -sOutputFile=gs-reencoded.pdf gs-reencoded.ps
% from Nimbus Sans (URW++, the base 35 fonts of Ghostscript; embedding in a document is
% what the font licence allows), re-encoded so that the codes are not the characters'.
% The invented text is the whole content.
/ReEncode { /enc exch def /base exch def /newname exch def
  base findfont dup length dict begin
  { 1 index /FID ne { def } { pop pop } ifelse } forall
  /Encoding enc def
  newname currentdict end definefont pop } def
/MyEnc 256 array def 0 1 255 { MyEnc exch /.notdef put } for
MyEnc 1 /H put MyEnc 2 /e put MyEnc 3 /l put MyEnc 4 /o put MyEnc 5 /space put MyEnc 6 /W put MyEnc 7 /r put MyEnc 8 /d put
MyEnc 9 /eacute put MyEnc 10 /Euro put MyEnc 11 /fi put MyEnc 12 /ntilde put MyEnc 13 /two put MyEnc 14 /zero put
/MyFont /NimbusSans-Regular MyEnc ReEncode
/MyFont findfont 20 scalefont setfont
72 700 moveto (\001\002\003\003\004\005\006\004\007\003\010) show
72 670 moveto (\011\012 \013 \014 \015\016) show
showpage
